WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:07.260
Narrator: One gala, start to finish. Four people at a nonprofit and one sponsor, on the real app, with invented data.

2
00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:14.400
Mei: Seven months to the gala. Let's set it up.

3
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:19.930
Narrator: Mei, the gala admin, signs in with a six-digit code from her email. No passwords.

4
00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.580
Mei: Sponsors name their guests by April twenty-third.

5
00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:35.560
Narrator: Gala information holds the date, the venue and the deadlines. Emails and the sponsor portal read them from here.

6
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.550
Mei: Every package says how many seats come with it.

7
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.030
Narrator: Each sponsorship level has its price, and how many guests it includes.

8
00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.020
Mei: Give Lively sold more overnight. One upload and they're in.

9
00:00:49.470 --> 00:00:57.830
Narrator: Mei uploads last night's export, links its pages and ticket types once, and imports. Twenty-seven new orders. The close calls wait for a person.

10
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:13.540
Daniel: Acme still owes twenty-five thousand dollars, and five seats have no names.

11
00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:18.170
Narrator: Daniel is a relationship manager: the role Pursuit testers sign in as.

12
00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:22.670
Daniel: Jordan's check came in the mail. Recording it.

13
00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:29.950
Narrator: Check ten forty-two, for twelve thousand five hundred dollars, with the day it arrived. No card or bank details, ever.

14
00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.860
Daniel: Every email waits for a person. This one's right. Send.

15
00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:44.150
Narrator: The guest list reminder was drafted on its own. It goes out only when staff approve it.

16
00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.040
Jordan: There's our link.

17
00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:55.700
Narrator: Jordan, at Acme, gets the reminder. The button opens Acme's private sponsor portal.

18
00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:59.900
Jordan: Our seats, and the check already shows.

19
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:04.660
Narrator: Five of ten guests named so far, and the payment shows as partially paid.

20
00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.690
Jordan: Avery's coming. Vegetarian.

21
00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:13.490
Narrator: A name, the organization for the badge, an email, and food and access needs.

22
00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.490
Jordan: Seven named. The last three by April twenty-third.

23
00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.350
Narrator: Riley Chen too. Seven of ten named.

24
00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.340
Daniel: Names and titles check out. Reviewed.

25
00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:46.910
Narrator: Staff review every name a sponsor adds. In the portal, Jordan now sees: confirmed by the Nonprofit.

26
00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:53.880
Daniel: Acme's guests sit together.

27
00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:58.060
Narrator: Avery and Riley at the same table, and their badges marked ready.

28
00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.340
Daniel: The E.D. invited Sam. Comp seat.

29
00:03:09.790 --> 00:03:14.360
Narrator: Sam Ortega, the Executive Director's guest. No payment, and no sponsor.

30
00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:23.670
Daniel: Sam shows this at the door.

31
00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:30.930
Narrator: Daniel reads the invitation, then sends it. Sam's QR code is for one seat, and works until the morning after the gala.

32
00:03:43.810 --> 00:03:45.240
Mei: Badges, off to print.

33
00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:47.500
Narrator: One file for the badge printer.

34
00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:56.390
Kenji: Doors at six. The iPad's ready.

35
00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:03.350
Narrator: Kenji, a volunteer, signs the iPad in with his own code. Five hundred seventy-seven guests, synced live.

36
00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:11.830
Kenji: Welcome, Avery!

37
00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:15.650
Narrator: Search, tap, checked in. Undo stays up for ten seconds.

38
00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.090
Kenji: Scanned. You're all set.

39
00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:25.830
Narrator: Sam holds up the ticket. The iPad's camera reads it, and says who came in.

40
00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:29.200
Kenji: Not on the list, but Mei says yes.

41
00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:32.530
Narrator: A walk-in, added as an exception, with who approved it.

42
00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:41.940
Kenji: No Wi-Fi? Keep going.

43
00:04:42.390 --> 00:04:47.100
Narrator: With the Wi-Fi down, check-ins wait on the iPad, and send themselves once it's back.

44
00:04:57.570 --> 00:04:58.620
Mei: Everyone's in.

45
00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.590
Narrator: The dashboard counts arrivals live from the door.

46
00:05:03.190 --> 00:05:04.450
Mei: For the thank-you notes.

47
00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:09.380
Narrator: Who came, one row per guest. Gala admins only, since it holds emails.

48
00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:20.920
Narrator: Everyone here is invented. Try it yourself: the Gala Tester Quickstart has your sign-in, and five task cards.

